  "reason": "The records repeatedly describe molecular-dynamics tensile loading of the closely related FCC CoNiCrFeMn/Cantor alloy over multiple temperatures at high strain rate. They establish partial-dislocation nucleation, stacking-fault formation, local HCP-associated structures, a yield stress drop, and thermally assisted nucleation causing earlier yielding and lower strength. Other records supply higher-rate MD loading and general thermal activation of dislocations. Thus an expert could plausibly propose the later temperature-, orientation-, and strain-rate-dependent tensile MD study and its partial-dislocation/stacking-fault mechanism. The precise crystallographic directions, vacancy-cluster initiation, negligible rate sensitivity, and absence of twinning or bulk transformation are not directly anticipated, but these are refinements rather than a substantial new intervention concept."
